message: "If you use this graph, please cite it as below."
title: "R(9,11) >= 620: a 619-vertex Ramsey graph"
version: "1.1"
authors:
  - family-names: Chrisbacher
    given-names: Peter J.
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "A graph on 619 vertices with no K9 and no independent set of size 11, improving the lower bound for the Ramsey number R(9,11) to 620. Built by Theorem 3 of Xu, Shao and Radziszowski (SIAM J. Discrete Math. 25 (2011)) from blocks of Google Research's R(9,11) graph, with a larger 20-vertex common induced subgraph and a valid split, and checked by independently written exact programs. Version 1.0 (R(9,11) >= 618) is kept as history."
keywords: [Ramsey numbers, lower bounds, graph construction]
